WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.900
- The problem is 98% of people

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.140
are sitting on 50/50
their whole fucking life,

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.640
which means they're zero-zero.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.290
So when you're 50/50, you get one day,

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.910
and anything else is you're just fucking

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.960
sitting and bullshitting.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.093
So fucking flip a coin, pick
the one, never look back.

00:00:16.093 --> 00:00:18.453
(waves rolling)

00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:19.286
(electronic noises)

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:20.540
- [Woman] Anybody out there?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.973
I have a big life decision to make,

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.343
between two choices.

00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:30.156
(electronic noises)

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:31.883
How do I know which way to go?

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.683
- You'll never know what the
alternative would have been.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.200
You pick one and you never
ever, ever even consider

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.123
to look back.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.320
- [Woman] Do you have any
quick piece of advice?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.552
- [Man] What should I do?

00:00:46.552 --> 00:00:47.385
Should I do?

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:48.218
- [Man] I don't know which one to pick.

00:00:48.218 --> 00:00:49.440
- [Man] What should I do?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.881
- [Interviewer] So what
should we do Gary V?

00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:51.714
- [Man] What should I do?

00:00:51.714 --> 00:00:52.547
- [Interviewer] What should people do?

00:00:52.547 --> 00:00:55.040
- Until you go through it, you won't know.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.230
I always play this out.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.600
Let's say when you go to heaven,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.430
they can show you what would've happened

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.640
'cause that's the only
way you'd ever see it.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.300
Let's just say

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.480
what people don't understand is,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.270
oh, Becca, you made the wrong call.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.350
You should've went to grad school

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.750
instead of that opportunity

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.330
or this company instead of that company.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.470
But you'll never believe it.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:17.040
You should've went to
VaynerMedia and it was perfect

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.730
and you rose like the phoenix

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.310
and you were the head of all sound

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.320
and everything went great.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.560
But then you had to go
to Virginia on business

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.760
and you got hit by a
car and you died at 31.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.423
That's life.

00:01:32.643 --> 00:01:35.643
(calm instrumental)

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.720
I passed on Uber as an investor
twice in the beginning.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.320
If I did my normal 25, $50,000 check,

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.290
I would've made $400 million

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.870
which means I might've went to China

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.600
for a keynote two years ago

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.320
which means I could've
got hit by a fucking bus.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.690
I really believe in that shit.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:58.050
You just don't know.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.143
You think you know but
that is not how life works.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.810
So, to look at two ideas and
think you can practically

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.963
make a good decision is laughable.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.118
Literally flip a coin.

00:02:14.118 --> 00:02:15.330
(coin flipping)

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.240
Just pick the one that feels
better right that second.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.010
And make it about you

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.330
because usually what kids
struggle with is the decision

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.170
they want to do

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.590
versus the decision that they
think they're supposed to do

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.033
based on the other voices.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.140
You know, I think everybody
who's listening right now

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.110
if you wanna set yourself up for success,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.905
ask yourself how much risk you've taken

00:02:36.905 --> 00:02:40.290
in the first 10, 15, 20,
30, 40 years of your life.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.610
You're gonna figure it out by tasting it.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.950
Should I eat this cherry?

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:44.863
Will I like it?

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.060
The right strategy is to
fucking eat the cherry.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.930
Right?

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.983
Moving is important.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.640
'Cause you can change the course.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.820
You can't overthink it up front.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.120
Right?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.210
You just can't.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.170
Like, we're always wrong.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.490
A lot of people make the wrong decision.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.480
No matter what I say to
your question right now

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.410
and they're scared,
they'll continue to be,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.310
they won't do, they won't put in the work

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.731
or they'll be fearful
or whatever it may be

00:03:10.731 --> 00:03:12.060
and they'll lose.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.490
I mean, a lot of people lose.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.530
A lot, a lot, a lot, a lot of people lose.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.940
The way to really eliminate fear

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.400
is by not giving a fuck
about anybody's opinion.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.290
My losses are mine.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.220
I'll deal with them myself.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.560
I don't need your two cents.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.580
You're losing plenty on your own.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.630
If you don't give a fuck
about what people think,

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:30.760
you can do everything.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.730
But the quicker you
start, the quicker you do.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.403
I think people dwell.

00:03:37.345 --> 00:03:40.750
And I think dwelling
is the wrong strategy.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.790
I don't even respect my losses.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.350
I don't even give them the time

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.920
to teach me anything.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.027
I fucking look 'em in
the face and just go,

00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:47.860
"Fuck you,"

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.693
and I keep going.

00:03:48.693 --> 00:03:50.610
Think one time for one hour,

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.070
make the decision and go.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:52.903
I don't wanna hear you

00:03:52.903 --> 00:03:54.450
fucking complaining about it everyday.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.360
And I mean that.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.990
Way too many of you dwell on your losses.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.120
It's holding you back.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.430
Too many people make a decision

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.160
and then cry about their
decision every fucking second.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.166
You made a fucking decision.

00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:06.738
Own it, live it, sleep in that bed.

00:04:06.738 --> 00:04:07.980
Shit's over.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.960
You lost.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.073
Move the fuck on.

00:04:11.025 --> 00:04:11.858
(birds chirping)

00:04:11.858 --> 00:04:12.900
Literally flip a coin.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.628
Guys, the only thing I'm
hedging against is regret.

00:04:15.628 --> 00:04:19.173
That's what you need to be careful of.

00:04:19.173 --> 00:04:20.423
Regret's scary.

00:04:24.069 --> 00:04:25.600
Regret.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:26.800
And that's what most people do.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.370
They build a life that leads to regret.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.160
Nobody old and about to die
talks about what they did.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.933
They talk about what they didn't do.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.750
And you're in the best spot right now.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.490
You're in the best spot you'll ever be.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.890
Straight up.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.930
This is the time to be most thoughtful

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.733
but everybody wants you to
figure out your life now.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.993
Your parents don't have
their lives figured out.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.290
This is the time to taste

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.040
and put yourself in good positions.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.680
You could do everything wrong

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.100
for the next 10 years of your life

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.323
and be young as fuck.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.400
And have unlimited time
to do anything you want.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:12.115
(serene instrumental)

00:05:12.115 --> 00:05:12.948
- [Woman] Thank you Gary.

00:05:12.948 --> 00:05:14.230
Now I know which way to go.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.650
(waves crashing)

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.460
By the way, it was tails.

